            <ArticleTitle>Spontaneous intracranial hypotension with pachymeningeal enhancement on MRI.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1628-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Spontaneous intracranial hypotension (SIH) is a rarely reported syndrome of spontaneously occurring postural cephalalgia associated with low CSF pressure. We report a case of SIH in which MRI of the brain revealed diffuse symmetric pachymeningeal enhancement that resolved without specific therapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
